          <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">    Route </span><math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> to </span><math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">-th LLM
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Compute </span><math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}\leftarrow\arg\min_{\gamma}{F}(\gamma,P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}\leftarrow\arg\min_{\gamma}{F}(\gamma,P)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\leftarrow Q\setminus P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∖</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\leftarrow Q\setminus P</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span><span id="alg1.l9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in Y</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l9.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l9.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">do</span><span id="alg1.l9.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">


</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   Estimate </span><math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{d}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{d}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> and </span><math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="alg1.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall~i\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.477em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall~i\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l10.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   Compute </span><math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\alpha}\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma^{*}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\alpha}\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma^{*}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall~i\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.477em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall~i\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l11.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   Route </span><math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> to </span><math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=\arg\max_{i}({\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\alpha}\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma^{*}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=\arg\max_{i}({\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\alpha}\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma^{*}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l12.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Methodology</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To tackle the challenges, our algorithm estimates the performance scores and costs efficiently using a historical dataset (Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Efficient Performance and Cost Estimation ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>), and learns a routing strategy from a small subset of observed queries (of size <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon|Q|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon|Q|</annotation></semantics></math>) to guide future query routing (Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Online Routing from Observed Queries ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Efficient Performance and Cost Estimation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our solution to estimate <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is to leverage a historical dataset <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> with a specialized data structure that supports efficient similarity-based retrieval. Specifically, let <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{j,a_{j},d_{j},g_{j}\}_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{j,a_{j},d_{j},g_{j}\}_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the response vector generated by the <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> LLMs for query <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j},g_{j}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j},g_{j}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the corresponding performance scores and costs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For any incoming query <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in Q</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply a classic ANNS method over <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> in the embedding space, such as DiskANN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> and HNSW <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, to select the most similar data points for estimation.
This yields a set of approximate nearest neighbors for <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{j}\subset D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{j}\subset D</annotation></semantics></math>.
The estimated performance score <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{d}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{d}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> and cost <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> for LLM <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> are then computed as the mean over these neighbors: <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{d}_{ij}=\frac{1}{|R_{j}|}\sum_{q\in R_{j}}d_{iq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{d}_{ij}=\frac{1}{|R_{j}|}\sum_{q\in R_{j}}d_{iq}</annotation></semantics></math>,  <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}_{ij}=\frac{1}{|R_{j}|}\sum_{q\in R_{j}}g_{iq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}_{ij}=\frac{1}{|R_{j}|}\sum_{q\in R_{j}}g_{iq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">One significant advantage of using ANNS compared with other training-based approaches is the ease of updating the historical dataset <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> to adopt various deployment configurations without requiring model retraining. This is particularly advantageous for LLM-serving providers, as it incurs almost no additional deployment overhead.
Online systems can naturally collect and record diverse user queries, which can be directly used to maintain and expand the dataset <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.
Although collecting ground-truth performance scores and costs typically requires human or automated evaluation, many providers already integrate such mechanisms (e.g., quality feedback from users) in their systems <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>)</cite>.
Furthermore, widely used ANNS algorithms in practice, such as HNSW<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            We note that many other choices are interchangeable here, e.g. see <a href="https://ann-benchmarks.com" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://ann-benchmarks.com</a>.</span></span></span>, use a graph-based indexing structure, making it substantially more efficient in search complexity (typical <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log|D|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log|D|)</annotation></semantics></math> in practice) compared to traditional instance-based methods like exact K-Nearest Neighbor (KNN, <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(|D|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(|D|)</annotation></semantics></math>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>)</cite>, achieving significant speedup in search time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Online Routing from Observed Queries</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With the approximate features <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{d}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{d}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, we propose an online routing algorithm in <a href="#alg1" title="In 2 Background and Formal Problem Setup ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Approximate LP with Control Parameter.</span>
The first step is to approximate the original MILP using the estimated features <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{d}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{d}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In addition, we introduce a control parameter <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> into the objective, leading to the formulation in <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.2 Online Routing from Observed Queries ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. The inclusion of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> does not affect the optimal solution structure – it simply scales the objective value.
In fact, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a control parameter to ensure generalizability, which is discussed in <a href="#S4" title="4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:110.4pt;">
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j\in Q}\sum_{i\in[M]}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\alpha}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j\in Q}\sum_{i\in[M]}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\alpha}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{s.t. }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext mathsize="0.900em">s.t.</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{s.t. }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}\leq B_{i},~\forall i," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.477em">,</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}\leq B_{i},~\forall i,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E2Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i}x_{ij}\leq 1,~\forall j," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.477em">,</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i}x_{ij}\leq 1,~\forall j,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E2Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{ij}\in\{0,1\},~\forall i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.477em">,</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{ij}\in\{0,1\},~\forall i,j</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:110.4pt;">
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E3X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j\in Q}\sum_{i\in[M]}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\alpha}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j\in Q}\sum_{i\in[M]}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\alpha}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E3Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{s.t. }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext mathsize="0.900em">s.t.</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{s.t. }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}\leq B_{i},~\forall i," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.477em">,</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}\leq B_{i},~\forall i,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E3Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i}x_{ij}\leq 1,~\forall j," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.477em">,</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i}x_{ij}\leq 1,~\forall j,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E3Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\displaystyle x_{ij}\in[0,1]},~\forall i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.477em">,</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\displaystyle x_{ij}\in[0,1]},~\forall i,j</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:117.3pt;">
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E4X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in[M]}\gamma_{i}B_{i}+\sum_{j\in Q}\beta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in[M]}\gamma_{i}B_{i}+\sum_{j\in Q}\beta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E4Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{s.t. }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext mathsize="0.900em">s.t.</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{s.t. }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{j}\geq{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\alpha}\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma_{i},~\forall i,j," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.477em">,</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{j}\geq{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\alpha}\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma_{i},~\forall i,j,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E4Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{i}\geq 0,\hskip 9.24994pt\beta_{j}\geq 0,~\forall i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="1.097em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.477em">,</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{i}\geq 0,\hskip 9.24994pt\beta_{j}\geq 0,~\forall i,j</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dual LP under Relaxation.</span>
Let <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{max}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the max performance score across all queries,
and let <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <em id="S3.SS2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">offline approximate optimum</em> obtained by solving <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.2 Online Routing from Observed Queries ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> removed.
When the ratio <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}_{opt}/s_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}_{opt}/s_{max}</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{opt}/s_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{opt}/s_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>) is sufficiently large as <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q|</annotation></semantics></math> grows, which commonly holds in practice, particularly in high-volume settings, the optimal value to the relaxed LP closely approximates that of the original MILP. <span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            In our experiments, the optimality gap between the relaxed LP and the MILP is only 0.016% on SPROUT.</span></span></span> This is formalized in Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> with further discussion in <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Discussion on Our Theoretical Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.
Based on this observation, we apply LP relaxation to <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.2 Online Routing from Observed Queries ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, allowing <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> to take fractional values in <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
This yields the relaxed approximate LP in <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Online Routing from Observed Queries ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> with its dual given in <a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.2 Online Routing from Observed Queries ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Routing via Learned <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
By complementary slackness, if <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal solution to <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Online Routing from Observed Queries ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and (<math id="S3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>) is optimal solution to its dual, then <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{ij}&gt;0\Leftrightarrow\beta_{j}=\underset{i}{\max}~(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>max</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑖</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{ij}&gt;0\Leftrightarrow\beta_{j}=\underset{i}{\max}~(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
This implies that, at optimality, the dual objective can be expressed as a function parameterized by <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{F}(\gamma)=\sum_{i}\gamma_{i}B_{i}+\sum_{j}\underset{i}{\max}~(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>max</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑖</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{F}(\gamma)=\sum_{i}\gamma_{i}B_{i}+\sum_{j}\underset{i}{\max}~(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, ideally, given the offline optimal solution <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, each query <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> should be routed to the LLM <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\hat{g}_{ij}\gamma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
While it is infeasible to compute such a global offline solution in an online setting, this formalization motivates us to treat <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> as a set of routing weights applied across all LLMs to assist the routing process.
Building on this insight, we adapt this idea to the online setting: we learn an estimated set of weights <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> from the first <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=\epsilon|Q|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=\epsilon|Q|</annotation></semantics></math> queries.
The procedure in <a href="#alg1" title="In 2 Background and Formal Problem Setup ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> reflects this idea exactly where its first stage is to learn an optimal <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes dual objective <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{F}(\gamma,P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{F}(\gamma,P)</annotation></semantics></math> over the observed queries:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{F}(\gamma,P)=\epsilon\sum_{i}\gamma_{i}B_{i}+\sum_{j\in P}\underset{i}{\max}~(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\gamma_{i}\hat{g}_{ij})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>max</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑖</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{F}(\gamma,P)=\epsilon\sum_{i}\gamma_{i}B_{i}+\sum_{j\in P}\underset{i}{\max}~(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\gamma_{i}\hat{g}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">For each query <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in P</annotation></semantics></math>, the estimated features <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{d}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{d}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> for all models will be calculated and recorded to solve for <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since this stage requires only a small fraction of the total queries (<math id="S3.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math>), random routing is adopted, which may leave some queries in the waiting queue (lines 3, 5-6 in <a href="#alg1" title="In 2 Background and Formal Problem Setup ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) to improve the generalizability without degrading overall performance.
This approach aligns precisely with the core idea of PAC learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, where uniform and unbiased routing ensures the learned weights <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> generalize to the subsequent routing stage.
We formalize this in Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
Let the remaining queries be <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=Q\setminus{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=Q\setminus{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the second stage, the learned weights <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> are used to route each incoming query <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in Y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically, each query is directly assigned to the LLM that maximizes the score <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\gamma_{i}^{*}\hat{g}_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\gamma_{i}^{*}\hat{g}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> (line 12 in <a href="#alg1" title="In 2 Background and Formal Problem Setup ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
If the selected LLM has exhausted its budget, the query is placed in a queue to await execution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Compared to existing methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>, which often
involve repeated heavy computations, our algorithm is significantly more efficient.
It performs optimization only once over a small subset of queries, making it scalable for deployment in high-volume settings.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Theoretical Guarantees</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the following main theorem, we show that our algorithm achieves a competitive ratio close to <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> compared to the offline opt <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>, under natural assumptions (see <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Discussion on Our Theoretical Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> for discussion).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any given query set <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> with random arrival order, <a href="#alg1" title="In 2 Background and Formal Problem Setup ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> satisfies
<math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{alg}}{C_{opt}}\geq 1-O(\epsilon+\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{alg}}{C_{opt}}\geq 1-O(\epsilon+\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>
assuming
<math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{max}</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum performance score obtained for any query, and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net defined over all possible routing strategies <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To establish this theorem, we introduce the following necessary but mild assumption (see <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Discussion on Our Theoretical Assumptions ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> for a detailed discussion) and auxiliary lemmas.
The key intuition behind approximating features of one query <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> using a different query <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is that the error between their feature values remains bounded, as long as their embedding representations are close.
We formalize this as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any query <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j,j^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j,j^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a value <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that if <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\textsc{Emb}(j)-\textsc{Emb}(j^{\prime})||_{2}\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Emb</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Emb</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\textsc{Emb}(j)-\textsc{Emb}(j^{\prime})||_{2}\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall~i\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall~i\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-O(\delta))d_{ij^{\prime}}\leq{d}_{ij}\leq(1+O(\delta))d_{ij^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-O(\delta))d_{ij^{\prime}}\leq{d}_{ij}\leq(1+O(\delta))d_{ij^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-O(\delta))g_{ij^{\prime}}\leq{g}_{ij}\leq(1+O(\delta))g_{ij^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-O(\delta))g_{ij^{\prime}}\leq{g}_{ij}\leq(1+O(\delta))g_{ij^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{Emb}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Emb</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{Emb}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the embedding function of an embedding model.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This approximation strategy naturally introduces estimation errors.
Thus, it is necessary to quantify the discrepancy between the offline optimum <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math> and the offline approximate optimum <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We assume that for any query <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in Q</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a corresponding feasible set <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for estimation.
This yields the following Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> (proof in <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="~\forall j\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">~\forall j\in Q</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall j^{\prime}\in R_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall j^{\prime}\in R_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\textsc{Emb}(j)-\textsc{Emb}(j^{\prime})||_{2}\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Emb</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Emb</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\textsc{Emb}(j)-\textsc{Emb}(j^{\prime})||_{2}\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, and that <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> holds. Then, the offline approximate optimum <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}-C_{opt}}{C_{opt}}\right|\leq O(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}-C_{opt}}{C_{opt}}\right|\leq O(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#alg1" title="In 2 Background and Formal Problem Setup ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> yields the a set of routing results <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, from which we define the <em id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">estimated cumulative performance score</em> as <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}:=\sum_{j}\sum_{i}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}\hat{x}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}:=\sum_{j}\sum_{i}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}\hat{x}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The results <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}</annotation></semantics></math> are determined by the learned weights <math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and the budget limitation, and can be represented by <math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Accordingly, <math id="S4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as <math id="S4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}=\sum_{i}\min\{E_{i},\sum_{j}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}=\sum_{i}\min\{E_{i},\sum_{j}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the maximum feasible contribution under the budget <math id="S4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as: <math id="S4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}:=\sum_{j}^{k}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}:=\sum_{j}^{k}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\underset{k}{\argmax}\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">argmax</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑘</mo></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\underset{k}{\argmax}\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="~s.t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">~s.t.</annotation></semantics></math>  <math id="S4.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We further define the per-LLM estimated performance score <math id="S4.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est,i}:=\min\{E_{i},\sum_{j}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est,i}:=\min\{E_{i},\sum_{j}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Analyzing <math id="S4.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}</annotation></semantics></math> thus provides a way to evaluate the routing decisions <math id="S4.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. Unfortunately, directly assessing <math id="S4.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}</annotation></semantics></math> is challenging as it has a complex step function with discontinuities.
To facilitate analysis, we introduce a relaxed version <math id="S4.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\hat{C}}:=\sum_{i}\sum_{j}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\hat{C}}:=\sum_{i}\sum_{j}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, which removes the step function present in <math id="S4.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We further define per-model relaxed estimated performance score <math id="S4.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\hat{C}}_{i}:=\sum_{j}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\hat{C}}_{i}:=\sum_{j}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, and its counterpart over the observed query set <math id="S4.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S4.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\hat{C}}_{i}(P):=\sum_{j\in P}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\hat{C}}_{i}(P):=\sum_{j\in P}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that for any <math id="S4.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in P</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="S4.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})=1</annotation></semantics></math> if the index <math id="S4.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> randomly selected in the first stage of the algorithm equals <math id="S4.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise, <math id="S4.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">By removing the discontinuous step function, the analysis becomes tractable.
A key requirement for ensuring the performance of the algorithm is the generalizability of estimated routing weights <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> on the remaining queries <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.
To show this, we first prove that the performance disparity between <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\hat{C}}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\hat{C}}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> and its expected value <math id="S4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon{\hat{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon{\hat{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\hat{C}}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\hat{C}}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}|</annotation></semantics></math>, is bounded.
Since directly bounding this gap over all possible values of <math id="S4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is infeasible due to the infinite parameter space, we use an <em id="S4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="S4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>)</cite> <math id="S4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> (formally defined in <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (ϵ-Net []). ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) to reduce to a discrete covering set of routing rules, over which we apply a union bound.
We then extend the analysis to arbitrary <math id="S4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> values by rounding to <math id="S4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>.
The cumulative error over <math id="S4.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded in Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> (proof in <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>):</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net and assume that
<math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall~i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall~i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|\leq z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|\leq z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
then
<math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}z_{i}\leq O(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}z_{i}\leq O(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The following Lemma demonstrates the generalizability of <math id="S4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> on remaining queries <math id="S4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> (proof in <a href="#A2.SS4" title="B.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>). This Lemma highlights the role of the control parameter <math id="S4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> in our algorithm: it serves as a bridge to connect the cost and performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="~\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">~\forall i</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\sum_{j\in P}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})|\leq O(z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\sum_{j\in P}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})|\leq O(z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exists a control parameter <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i</annotation></semantics></math>, (1) <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|\leq z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|\leq z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and (2) <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon E_{i}|\leq O(z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon E_{i}|\leq O(z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">This connection further translates the cost constraint (<math id="S4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>) to a performance guarantee, which establishes the generalizability of <math id="S4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to the remaining queries <math id="S4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, as formalized in Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net. If <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}(Y)\geq(1-O(\epsilon))C_{est}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}(Y)\geq(1-O(\epsilon))C_{est}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the results above, we can prove our main <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (proof in <a href="#A2.SS6" title="B.6 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>
The main results on RouterBench, SPROUT, and Open LLM Leaderboard v2 are under a total budget equal to the cost of the cheapest model, split across models based on the cost efficiency. Here, Perf represents the <em id="S4.T1.14" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Performance</em>, PPC represents <em id="S4.T1.15" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Performance per Cost</em>, Tput represents <em id="S4.T1.16" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Throughput</em>, and RP denotes <em id="S4.T1.17" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Relative Performance</em> compared with offline approximate optimum (<math id="S4.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>).
