<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Budget.</span>
Our algorithm aims to improve routing performance under limited budgets in high-volume settings.
To simulate this high-volume, budget-constrained setting, we define the total budget based on the minimal cost required for a single model to process all test queries in the benchmark.
In the main setting, the budget is set to this minimal value.
To evaluate the robustness of our algorithms, we scale the budget by a factor ranging from 0.25 to 2.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">We consider multiple strategies for splitting the total budget across models.
In the main setting, we adopt a cost-efficiency-based split strategy.
As shown in Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix A More Experiment Details ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix A More Experiment Details ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix A More Experiment Details ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we report the average performance score, cost, and cost efficiency (Perf/Cost) of each model on the historical data across 3 benchmarks.
We observe a substantial disparity in cost efficiency across models.
For instance, for SPROUT, the most efficient model achieves a cost efficiency of 9722, while the least efficient only reaches 108, nearly a 100<math id="A1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> difference.
Directly allocating the budget based on cost efficiency is thus highly imbalanced, as it can result in nearly all resources being allocated to a single model.
Therefore, we adopt a smoothed version that allocates the budget proportionally to the square root of each model’s cost efficiency on the historical data, i.e., according to <math id="A1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{\textsc{Perf}}{\textsc{Cost}})^{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Perf</mtext><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Cost</mtext></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0.5</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{\textsc{Perf}}{\textsc{Cost}})^{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">In our robustness evaluations, we explore several alternative budget splitting strategies, including uniform split, random split, extreme split, cost-based split, and performance-based split.
In the cost-based split, the budget is allocated inversely proportional to the average cost.
However, due to the extreme cost imbalance across models (as also observed in the cost-efficiency-based split), we also adopt a smoothed variant that splits the budget proportional to <math id="A1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{1}{\textsc{Cost}})^{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Cost</mtext></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0.5</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{1}{\textsc{Cost}})^{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the performance-based split, the budget is directly assigned in proportion to the average performance scores of the models.
In the random split, the total budget is randomly allocated across LLMs, and the experiment is repeated 100 times to account for variability.
In the extreme split, 80% of the budget is assigned to the <math id="A1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> least cost-efficient models, and the remaining 20% is uniformly distributed among the others, where <math id="A1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> ranges from 1 to 5.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Optimization Implementation.</span>
We implement all optimization codes using the CVXPY <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> package.
For the one-time optimization step in our algorithm, we use the L-BFGS-B solver <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite>.
For BatchSplit, which involves solving a linear program for each batch, we adopt the HIGHS solver <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Devices.</span>
All experiments are conducted on a machine equipped with 16 CPUs and 32GB of memory.
For training the Roberta models used in the model-based baselines, we use two NVIDIA H200 GPUs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Proofs</h2>

<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="Thmdefinition1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-Net</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmdefinition1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a parameter <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and routing rule <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, a set <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi\subseteq[0,1]^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi\subseteq[0,1]^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net if, for any <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in[0,1]^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in[0,1]^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}\in\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}\in\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall~i,j,~|x_{ij}(\gamma)-x_{ij}(\gamma^{\prime})|\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall~i,j,~|x_{ij}(\gamma)-x_{ij}(\gamma^{\prime})|\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Discussion on Our Theoretical Assumptions</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce several mild assumptions in our theoretical analysis and provide justifications for each below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Random arrival order.</span>
We assume that the queries arrive in a random order, i.e., they can be picked adversarially, but their order is randomly permuted.
Note that this is a weaker requirement than assuming the queries are sampled i.i.d. from an unknown distribution. This is because if the queries are sampled i.i.d., then they also satisfy the random order requirement, and thus our assumption is weaker.
Furthermore, the random order model is also a popular assumption in many other online algorithms <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, since it typically allows one to go beyond worst-case hardness and obtain meaningful theoretical guarantees.
In practice, we perform robustness studies by changing the query order and observe that our algorithm still outperforms baselines; see <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Robustness ‣ 5 Evaluation ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">“<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math> is enough large” is practial.</span>
In <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we assume that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is naturally aligned with high-volume practical settings.
This is because <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the total number of queries <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q|</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas our lower bound assumption scales as a function of <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of LLMs.
Typically, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> can be thought of as a constant while <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q|</annotation></semantics></math>, the total number of queries, should grow over time.
Indeed, in all of our benchmarks, we observed that for <em id="A2.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">every query</em> <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal solution <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{ij}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{ij}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> (that is, the performance score achieved by the optimal solution on query <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>) satisfies <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in[M]}d_{ij}x_{ij}^{*}\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in[M]}d_{ij}x_{ij}^{*}\geq</annotation></semantics></math>0.462 consistently on Open LLM Leaderboard v2, 0.639 on RouterBench, and 0.887 on SPROUT, meaning that in practice, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math> scales as <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(Q)</annotation></semantics></math> (linear in <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>).
On the other hand, for constant <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g. we use <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.0001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.0001</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.025" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.025</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.025</annotation></semantics></math> in our main setting), our required lower bound is a polynomial of <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> (more specifically, it is close to a quadratic since <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> may depend exponentially in <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> but it is inside a logarithm).
However, we think of <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> as a constant. For example, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\leq 18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\leq 18</annotation></semantics></math> in all of our experiments. Even if <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is large, it is reasonable to assume that it is orders of magnitude smaller than <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q|</annotation></semantics></math> (in our experiments, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is on the order of thousands to tens of thousands, and in real-world systems, it can be much larger).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our assumption is further corroborated by the relaxation used in <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Efficient Performance and Cost Estimation ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, where if <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}}{s_{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}}{s_{max}}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large, the original MILP can be closely approximated by its fractional LP relaxation with only a negligible optimality gap.
We validate this in our main experiments over three benchmarks with the observed optimality gaps being: (i) 0.016% on SPROUT, (ii) 0.086% on RouterBench, and (iii) 0.3% on Open LLM Leaderboard v2.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Lastly, we remark that similar reasonable lower-bound assumptions have been made in prior work on the online matching problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, where it is commonly assumed that bids for the items are small compared to the total budget.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">“Estimating query features via similarity” is natural.</span>
The core intuition behind most previous literature on predictive LLM routing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>, <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>, <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>, which trains a model-based predictor on auxiliary datasets to estimate performance and cost of future queries, aligns with Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Specifically, these approaches assume that similar queries share similar routing-relevant features.
If no such relationship exists, then historical data would be uninformative, and it would be impossible to leverage historical data for effective future routing.
In this case, no meaningful inference can be made without directly querying the LLMs, and routing decisions degenerate to random selection.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">One may argue that useful routing information can still be obtained by querying only a subset of LLMs.
This idea is echoed in works that adopt cascading strategies, where LLMs are queried sequentially based on their observed capabilities on historical data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>.
However, these approaches also fundamentally rely on a related assumption: LLMs that perform well on historical data or benchmarks are likely to perform well on future queries.
Furthermore, these methods introduce significant latency and computational overhead, as they may consume substantial token budgets before reaching the optimal LLM.
This makes them impractical for high-volume online routing scenarios with tight token budgets and low-latency requirements.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">If no useful routing information can be inferred from historical data, no matter whether it is related to model capability or query features, then the system would need to query all LLMs to make informed routing decisions.
This is because in the worst case, under an adversary query targeting the LLM query order in the system, all LLMs may present extremely low performance, except the last LLM.
In this situation, no strategy can be adopted to improve overall routing performance without assessing all LLMs.
Therefore, it is important and natural to establish our assumption or use a related notion, e.g., Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, that links historical information with future queries to obtain meaningful routing information and improve routing performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem2a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="~\forall j\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">~\forall j\in Q</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall j^{\prime}\in R_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall j^{\prime}\in R_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\textsc{Emb}(j)-\textsc{Emb}(j^{\prime})||_{2}\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Emb</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Emb</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\textsc{Emb}(j)-\textsc{Emb}(j^{\prime})||_{2}\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, and that <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> holds. Then, the offline approximate optimum <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}-C_{opt}}{C_{opt}}\right|\leq O(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}-C_{opt}}{C_{opt}}\right|\leq O(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the optimal solution to <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> the optimal solution to <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1: <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{opt}\geq\hat{C}_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{opt}\geq\hat{C}_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. We have</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}-C_{opt}}{C_{opt}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}-C_{opt}}{C_{opt}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}-\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}-\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}(\hat{d}_{ij}-{d}_{ij})x_{1ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}(\hat{d}_{ij}-{d}_{ij})x_{1ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}(\frac{1}{|R_{j}|}\sum_{q\in R_{j}}d_{ik}-d_{ij})x_{1ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}(\frac{1}{|R_{j}|}\sum_{q\in R_{j}}d_{ik}-d_{ij})x_{1ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left|O(\delta)\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left|O(\delta)\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq O(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq O(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second inequality follows from the fact that <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}\sum_{i}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}\leq\sum_{j}\sum_{i}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}\sum_{i}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}\leq\sum_{j}\sum_{i}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal solution to <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the fourth inequality follows <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2: <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{opt}&lt;\hat{C}_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{opt}&lt;\hat{C}_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. We have</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}-C_{opt}}{C_{opt}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}-C_{opt}}{C_{opt}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}-\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}-\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}(\hat{d}_{ij}-{d}_{ij})x_{2ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}(\hat{d}_{ij}-{d}_{ij})x_{2ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}(\frac{1}{|R_{j}|}\sum_{q\in R_{j}}d_{ik}-d_{ij})x_{2ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}(\frac{1}{|R_{j}|}\sum_{q\in R_{j}}d_{ik}-d_{ij})x_{2ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left|O(\delta)\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left|O(\delta)\frac{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}}{\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq O(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq O(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second inequality uses the fact that <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}\leq\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}\leq\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal solution to <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the fourth inequality follows <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and the final inequality follows <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}\leq\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{2ij}\leq\sum_{j}\sum_{i}{d}_{ij}x_{1ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem3a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net and assume that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall~i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall~i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|\leq z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|\leq z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}z_{i}\leq O\left(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}z_{i}\leq O\left(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Inspired by the techniques used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, we first prove that, under the given setting, the partial performance score can be accurately estimated with high probability.
Specifically, for each <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, we evaluate the following probability</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|&gt;z_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|&gt;z_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that, for any <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in P</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance satisfies <span id="A2.SS3.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Var</span>[<math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>] <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq\frac{1}{|Q|}||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq\frac{1}{|Q|}||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{j\in P}\textsc{Var}[\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Var</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in P}\textsc{Var}[\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>] <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq\epsilon||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq\epsilon||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By applying Bernstein’s inequality, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|&gt;z_{i})\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{z_{i}^{2}/2}{\epsilon||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}+\frac{z_{i}}{3}\alpha s_{max}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|&gt;z_{i})\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{z_{i}^{2}/2}{\epsilon||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}+\frac{z_{i}}{3}\alpha s_{max}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We aim to find such <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> that this probability is below a given tolerance <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.
Set RHS as <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and solve for <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}=\frac{\frac{2}{3}\log\frac{2}{\tau}\alpha s_{max}+\sqrt{(\frac{2}{3}\log\frac{2}{\tau}\alpha s_{max}+8\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}}}{2}\leq\frac{2}{3}\log\frac{2}{\tau}\alpha s_{max}+\sqrt{2\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}=\frac{\frac{2}{3}\log\frac{2}{\tau}\alpha s_{max}+\sqrt{(\frac{2}{3}\log\frac{2}{\tau}\alpha s_{max}+8\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}}}{2}\leq\frac{2}{3}\log\frac{2}{\tau}\alpha s_{max}+\sqrt{2\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Without affecting the analysis, we define <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}=\frac{2}{3}\log\frac{2}{\tau}\alpha s_{max}+\sqrt{2\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}=\frac{2}{3}\log\frac{2}{\tau}\alpha s_{max}+\sqrt{2\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\epsilon/(M|\Phi|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\epsilon/(M|\Phi|)</annotation></semantics></math>, and use <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i}z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i}z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i}\frac{2}{3}\log\frac{2}{\tau}\alpha s_{max}+\sum_{i}\sqrt{2\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i}\frac{2}{3}\log\frac{2}{\tau}\alpha s_{max}+\sum_{i}\sqrt{2\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}||{\hat{C}}_{i}||_{2}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq O(M\log\frac{1}{\tau}\alpha s_{max})+\sum_{i}\sqrt{2\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}{\hat{C}}_{i}s_{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq O(M\log\frac{1}{\tau}\alpha s_{max})+\sum_{i}\sqrt{2\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}{\hat{C}}_{i}s_{max}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq O(\epsilon^{3}C_{opt}(1+\delta))+\sqrt{2M\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}{\hat{C}}s_{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq O(\epsilon^{3}C_{opt}(1+\delta))+\sqrt{2M\epsilon\log\frac{2}{\tau}{\hat{C}}s_{max}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq O(\epsilon^{3}C_{opt}(1+\delta))+O(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)})\sqrt{C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq O(\epsilon^{3}C_{opt}(1+\delta))+O(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)})\sqrt{C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq O\left(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq O\left(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem4a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="~\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">~\forall i</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\sum_{j\in P}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})|\leq O(z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\sum_{j\in P}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})|\leq O(z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exists a control parameter <math id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i</annotation></semantics></math>, (1) <math id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|\leq z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}|\leq z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and (2) <math id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon E_{i}|\leq O(z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\hat{C}}_{i}(P)-\epsilon E_{i}|\leq O(z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}:=\sum_{j\in P}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon\sum_{j}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}:=\sum_{j\in P}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon\sum_{j}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}:=\sum_{j\in P}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}:=\sum_{j\in P}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we aim to ensure the following two conditions hold: (1) <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha|M_{i}|\leq z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha|M_{i}|\leq z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and (2) <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha|H_{i}|\leq O(z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha|H_{i}|\leq O(z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, condition (1) holds trivially for any <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>; similarly, if <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, condition (2) also holds for any <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now consider the case where <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}\not=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}\not=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then it requires that <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\frac{z_{i}}{|M_{i}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\frac{z_{i}}{|M_{i}|}</annotation></semantics></math>, and when <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}\not=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}\not=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to have <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{|H_{i}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{|H_{i}|}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of indice <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}\not=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}\not=0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}\not=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}\not=0</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,1}=\begin{cases}\frac{z_{i}}{|M_{i}|}&amp;\text{if }M_{i}\neq 0\\
\infty&amp;\text{if }M_{i}=0\end{cases}\qquad V_{i,2}=\begin{cases}\frac{O(z_{i})}{|H_{i}|}&amp;\text{if }H_{i}\neq 0\\
\infty&amp;\text{if }H_{i}=0\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,1}=\begin{cases}\frac{z_{i}}{|M_{i}|}&amp;\text{if }M_{i}\neq 0\\
\infty&amp;\text{if }M_{i}=0\end{cases}\qquad V_{i,2}=\begin{cases}\frac{O(z_{i})}{|H_{i}|}&amp;\text{if }H_{i}\neq 0\\
\infty&amp;\text{if }H_{i}=0\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}:=\min\{V_{i,1},V_{i,2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}:=\min\{V_{i,1},V_{i,2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\inf_{i\in I}\{V_{i}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\inf_{i\in I}\{V_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, we find a control parameter <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that both conditions (1) and (2) are satisfied.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem5a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem5a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="Thmtheorem5a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net. If <math id="Thmtheorem5a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem5a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}(Y)\geq(1-O(\epsilon))C_{est}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}(Y)\geq(1-O(\epsilon))C_{est}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first prove that <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall~i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall~i</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> where</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}(\gamma^{*}):=\gamma_{i}^{*}B_{i}+\sum_{j}(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\gamma_{i}^{*}\hat{g}_{ij})x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}(\gamma^{*}):=\gamma_{i}^{*}B_{i}+\sum_{j}(\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}-\gamma_{i}^{*}\hat{g}_{ij})x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">From <a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.2 Online Routing from Observed Queries ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, it follows immediately that <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}F_{i}(\gamma^{*})=F(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}F_{i}(\gamma^{*})=F(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1:<span id="A2.SS5.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{*}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{*}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this case,</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}=\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},{\hat{C}}_{i}+\gamma_{i}^{*}(B_{i}-\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*}))\}-\min\{E_{i},{\hat{C}}_{i}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}=\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},{\hat{C}}_{i}+\gamma_{i}^{*}(B_{i}-\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*}))\}-\min\{E_{i},{\hat{C}}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">which follows <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est,i}=\min\{E_{i},{\hat{C}}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est,i}=\min\{E_{i},{\hat{C}}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We consider two sub-cases separately:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sub-case 1.1:<span id="A2.SS5.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}=\gamma_{i}^{*}(B_{i}-\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*}))\leq B_{i}-\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}=\gamma_{i}^{*}(B_{i}-\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*}))\leq B_{i}-\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Due to complementary slackness conditions over observed queries <math id="A2.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in P}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})=\epsilon B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in P}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})=\epsilon B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\sum_{j\in P}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})|=\epsilon|B_{i}-\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})|\leq O(z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\sum_{j\in P}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})|=\epsilon|B_{i}-\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})|\leq O(z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sub-case 1.2:<span id="A2.SS5.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A2.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})&gt;B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})&gt;B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We obtain,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}={\hat{C}}_{i}-E_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}={\hat{C}}_{i}-E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, it can be expanded and bounded as:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\hat{C}}_{i}-E_{i}=\frac{1}{\epsilon}(\sum_{j}\epsilon\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon E_{i})\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\hat{C}}_{i}-E_{i}=\frac{1}{\epsilon}(\sum_{j}\epsilon\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\epsilon E_{i})\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2:<span id="A2.SS5.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A2.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{*}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{*}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}={\hat{C}}_{i}-\min\{{\hat{C}}_{i},E_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}={\hat{C}}_{i}-\min\{{\hat{C}}_{i},E_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A2.SS5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, this difference <math id="A2.SS5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\hat{C}}_{i}-\min\{{\hat{C}}_{i},E_{i}\}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\hat{C}}_{i}-\min\{{\hat{C}}_{i},E_{i}\}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, we only consider the situation <math id="A2.SS5.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})&gt;B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})&gt;B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, leading to</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max\{{\hat{C}}_{i},F_{i}(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est,i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\hat{C}}_{i}-\min\{{\hat{C}}_{i},E_{i}\}\leq{\hat{C}}_{i}-E_{i}\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\hat{C}}_{i}-\min\{{\hat{C}}_{i},E_{i}\}\leq{\hat{C}}_{i}-E_{i}\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">which follows Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lower Bound on<span id="A2.SS5.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A2.SS5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
From Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we have,</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{est,i}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{est,i}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min\{{\hat{C}}_{i}-{\hat{C}}_{i}(P),E_{i}-\sum_{j\in P}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min\{{\hat{C}}_{i}-{\hat{C}}_{i}(P),E_{i}-\sum_{j\in P}\alpha\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\min\{(1-\epsilon){\hat{C}}_{i}-z_{i},(1-\epsilon)E_{i}-O(z_{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\min\{(1-\epsilon){\hat{C}}_{i}-z_{i},(1-\epsilon)E_{i}-O(z_{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-\epsilon)C_{est,i}-O(z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-\epsilon)C_{est,i}-O(z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where second inequality follows that <math id="A2.SS5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\hat{C}}_{i}(Y)-(1-\epsilon){\hat{C}}_{i}|\leq z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\hat{C}}_{i}(Y)-(1-\epsilon){\hat{C}}_{i}|\leq z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\hat{C}}_{i}-E_{i}|\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\hat{C}}_{i}-E_{i}|\leq\frac{O(z_{i})}{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Summing over all <math id="A2.SS5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we get <math id="A2.SS5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}(Y)\geq(1-\epsilon)C_{est}-\sum_{i}O(z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}(Y)\geq(1-\epsilon)C_{est}-\sum_{i}O(z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Due to the fact that <math id="A2.SS5.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}z_{i}\leq O\left(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}z_{i}\leq O\left(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we finally obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{est}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{est}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-\epsilon)C_{est}-O\left(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-\epsilon)C_{est}-O\left(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow C_{est}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow C_{est}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-O(\epsilon))C_{est}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-O(\epsilon))C_{est}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.6 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any given query set <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> with random arrival order, <a href="#alg1" title="In 2 Background and Formal Problem Setup ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> satisfies
<math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{alg}}{C_{opt}}\geq 1-O(\epsilon+\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{alg}}{C_{opt}}\geq 1-O(\epsilon+\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>
assuming
<math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{max}</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum performance score obtained for any query, and <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net defined over all possible routing strategies <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case <math id="A2.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}\in\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}\in\Phi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS6.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.
According to Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we have a union bound over <math id="A2.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>.
This union bound implies that with probability greater than <math id="A2.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}z_{i}\leq O(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}z_{i}\leq O(\epsilon^{2}\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}})</annotation></semantics></math> holds.
Therefore, we have that</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max\{{\hat{C}},F(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est}\leq\frac{1}{\epsilon}\sum_{i}z_{i}\Rightarrow\max\{{\hat{C}},F(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est}\leq O\left(\epsilon\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max\{{\hat{C}},F(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est}\leq\frac{1}{\epsilon}\sum_{i}z_{i}\Rightarrow\max\{{\hat{C}},F(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est}\leq O\left(\epsilon\sqrt{(1+\delta)C_{opt}{\hat{C}}/\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\delta)C_{opt}\geq{\hat{C}}/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\delta)C_{opt}\geq{\hat{C}}/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{{\hat{C}},F(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est}\leq O(\epsilon(1+\delta)C_{opt})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{{\hat{C}},F(\gamma^{*})\}-C_{est}\leq O(\epsilon(1+\delta)C_{opt})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By weak dualtiy, we have <math id="A2.I1.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}\leq\alpha\hat{C}_{opt}\leq F(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}\leq\alpha\hat{C}_{opt}\leq F(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, we have <math id="A2.I1.i1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}}{C_{opt}}\in[1-O(\delta),1+O(\delta)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\hat{C}_{opt}}{C_{opt}}\in[1-O(\delta),1+O(\delta)]</annotation></semantics></math> (from Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
Therefore, we obtain that <math id="A2.I1.i1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(1-O(\delta))C_{opt}-C_{est}\leq O(\epsilon(1+\delta)C_{opt})\Rightarrow C_{est}/\alpha\geq(1-O(\epsilon+\delta))C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(1-O(\delta))C_{opt}-C_{est}\leq O(\epsilon(1+\delta)C_{opt})\Rightarrow C_{est}/\alpha\geq(1-O(\epsilon+\delta))C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\delta)C_{opt}&lt;{\hat{C}}/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\delta)C_{opt}&lt;{\hat{C}}/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, by the same weak dualtiy, we have <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\hat{C}}-\alpha(1+O(\delta))C_{opt}\leq O(\epsilon{\hat{C}}/\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\hat{C}}-\alpha(1+O(\delta))C_{opt}\leq O(\epsilon{\hat{C}}/\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>,
which further implies that <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\hat{C}}\leq\alpha\frac{1+O(\delta)}{1-O(\epsilon)/\alpha}C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\hat{C}}\leq\alpha\frac{1+O(\delta)}{1-O(\epsilon)/\alpha}C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, we have <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(1+\delta)C_{opt}-C_{est}\leq O(\epsilon{\hat{C}})\Rightarrow C_{est}/\alpha\geq(1-O(\epsilon+\delta))C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(1+\delta)C_{opt}-C_{est}\leq O(\epsilon{\hat{C}})\Rightarrow C_{est}/\alpha\geq(1-O(\epsilon+\delta))C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can define <math id="A2.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{alg}:=\sum_{i}\min\{T_{i},\sum_{j}{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{alg}:=\sum_{i}\min\{T_{i},\sum_{j}{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}:=\sum_{j}^{t}{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}:=\sum_{j}^{t}{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\underset{t}{\argmax}\sum_{j}^{t}{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">argmax</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑡</mo></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\underset{t}{\argmax}\sum_{j}^{t}{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="~s.t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">~s.t.</annotation></semantics></math>  <math id="A2.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}^{t}{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}^{t}{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, we have <math id="A2.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}/\alpha=\sum_{i}\min\{{E}_{i}/\alpha,\sum_{j}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}/\alpha=\sum_{i}\min\{{E}_{i}/\alpha,\sum_{j}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{E}_{i}/\alpha=\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{E}_{i}/\alpha=\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\underset{k}{\argmax}\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">argmax</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑘</mo></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\underset{k}{\argmax}\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="~s.t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">~s.t.</annotation></semantics></math>  <math id="A2.SS6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}^{k}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be the largest <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
According to Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, for each <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-O(\delta))\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq(1+O(\delta))\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-O(\delta))\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq(1+O(\delta))\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}/(1-O(\delta))=(1+O(\delta))B_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}/(1-O(\delta))=(1+O(\delta))B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be the largest <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}^{k_{i}^{*}}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}^{k_{i}^{*}}\hat{g}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\leq B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Without loss of generalizability, assume <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{*}\geq k_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{*}\geq k_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, there exists a set of tail queries, <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which makes <a href="#A2.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ B.6 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> exceed <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by at most <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\delta)B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\delta)B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we define excess performance contributed by these tail queries as <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because the query order is random, we consider the expected excess performance</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})]=\frac{O(\delta)B_{i}}{B_{i}}E_{i}/\alpha=O(\delta)E_{i}/\alpha" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})]=\frac{O(\delta)B_{i}}{B_{i}}E_{i}/\alpha=O(\delta)E_{i}/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">and the variance satisfies <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{Var}[\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})]\leq O(\delta)||E_{i}/\alpha||_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{Var}[\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})]\leq O(\delta)||E_{i}/\alpha||_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using Bernstein’s inequality, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(|\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-O(\delta)E_{i}/\alpha|&gt;e_{i})\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{e_{i}^{2}/2}{O(\delta)||E_{i}/\alpha||_{2}^{2}+\frac{e_{i}}{3}s_{max}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(|\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-O(\delta)E_{i}/\alpha|&gt;e_{i})\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{e_{i}^{2}/2}{O(\delta)||E_{i}/\alpha||_{2}^{2}+\frac{e_{i}}{3}s_{max}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Follow Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, set RHS as <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon/(M|\Phi|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon/(M|\Phi|)</annotation></semantics></math>, use <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{opt}}{s_{max}}\geq\Omega(\frac{\alpha M\log(M|\Phi|/\epsilon)}{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)})</annotation></semantics></math>, and union bound for all <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, then with probability greater than <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}e_{i}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)O(\delta)C_{opt}E/\alpha^{2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}e_{i}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)O(\delta)C_{opt}E/\alpha^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">where we denote <math id="A2.SS6.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=\sum_{i}E_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=\sum_{i}E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Based on this, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\sum_{i}T_{i}-\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\sum_{i}T_{i}-\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left|\sum_{i}\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\sum_{i}\sum_{j}^{k_{i}^{*}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left|\sum_{i}\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\sum_{i}\sum_{j}^{k_{i}^{*}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left|(1+O(\delta))\sum_{i}\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\sum_{i}\sum_{j}^{k_{i}^{*}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left|(1+O(\delta))\sum_{i}\sum_{j}^{t_{i}^{*}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-\sum_{i}\sum_{j}^{k_{i}^{*}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left|O(\delta)\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha+(1+O(\delta))\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\sum_{i}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left|O(\delta)\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha+(1+O(\delta))\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\sum_{i}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left|O(\delta)\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha+(1+O(\delta))(O(\delta)E/\alpha+\sum_{i}e_{i})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left|O(\delta)\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha+(1+O(\delta))(O(\delta)E/\alpha+\sum_{i}e_{i})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(O(\delta)+O\left(\sqrt{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)O(\delta)C_{opt}/E}\right)\right)\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(O(\delta)+O\left(\sqrt{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)O(\delta)C_{opt}/E}\right)\right)\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(O(\delta)+O\left(\sqrt{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)O(\delta)/(1-O(\epsilon+\delta)\alpha)}\right)\right)\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(O(\delta)+O\left(\sqrt{\epsilon^{3}(1+\delta)O(\delta)/(1-O(\epsilon+\delta)\alpha)}\right)\right)\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(O(\delta)+O\left(\epsilon^{3/2}\sqrt{\delta/\alpha}\right)\right)\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(O(\delta)+O\left(\epsilon^{3/2}\sqrt{\delta/\alpha}\right)\right)\sum_{i}E_{i}/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the penultimate inequality follows <math id="A2.SS6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E/\alpha\geq C_{est}/\alpha\geq(1-O(\epsilon+\delta))C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E/\alpha\geq C_{est}/\alpha\geq(1-O(\epsilon+\delta))C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, it leads to <math id="A2.SS6.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C_{alg}-C_{est}/\alpha|\leq\left(O(\delta)+O\left(\epsilon^{3/2}\sqrt{\delta/\alpha}\right)\right)C_{est}/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{alg}-C_{est}/\alpha|\leq\left(O(\delta)+O\left(\epsilon^{3/2}\sqrt{\delta/\alpha}\right)\right)C_{est}/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because <math id="A2.SS6.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}/\alpha\geq(1-O(\epsilon+\delta))C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}/\alpha\geq(1-O(\epsilon+\delta))C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that <math id="A2.SS6.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{alg}}{C_{opt}}\geq 1-O(\epsilon+\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{alg}}{C_{opt}}\geq 1-O(\epsilon+\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case <math id="A2.SS6.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}\not\in\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}\not\in\Phi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS6.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.
As <math id="A2.SS6.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A2.SS6.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net, there exists an <math id="A2.SS6.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS6.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall~i,j,~|x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-x_{ij}(\gamma^{\prime})|\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall~i,j,~|x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-x_{ij}(\gamma^{\prime})|\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, we obtain</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*},P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*},P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq|{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{\prime},P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{\prime})|+|{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{\prime},P)-{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*},P)|+|\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{\prime})-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq|{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{\prime},P)-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{\prime})|+|{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{\prime},P)-{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*},P)|+|\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{\prime})-\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq z_{i}^{\prime}+\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*},P)+\epsilon^{2}{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq z_{i}^{\prime}+\epsilon{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*},P)+\epsilon^{2}{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq z_{i}^{\prime}+O(\epsilon^{2}{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq z_{i}^{\prime}+O(\epsilon^{2}{\hat{C}}_{i}(\gamma^{*}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for each <math id="A2.SS6.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-O(\delta)E_{i}(\gamma^{*})/\alpha|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})-O(\delta)E_{i}(\gamma^{*})/\alpha|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq|\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{\prime})-O(\delta)E_{i}(\gamma^{\prime})/\alpha|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq|\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{\prime})-O(\delta)E_{i}(\gamma^{\prime})/\alpha|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+|\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{\prime})-\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+|\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{\prime})-\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+|O(\delta)E_{i}(\gamma^{\prime})/\alpha-O(\delta)E_{i}(\gamma^{*})/\alpha|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+|O(\delta)E_{i}(\gamma^{\prime})/\alpha-O(\delta)E_{i}(\gamma^{*})/\alpha|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq e_{i}^{\prime}+\epsilon\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})+\epsilon O(\delta)E_{i}(\gamma^{*})/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq e_{i}^{\prime}+\epsilon\sum_{j\in A_{i}}\hat{d}_{ij}x_{ij}(\gamma^{*})+\epsilon O(\delta)E_{i}(\gamma^{*})/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq e_{i}^{\prime}+O(\epsilon\delta E_{i}(\gamma^{*})/\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq e_{i}^{\prime}+O(\epsilon\delta E_{i}(\gamma^{*})/\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">where, with slight abuse of notation, we use <math id="A2.SS6.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}(\gamma^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}(\gamma^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the value computed under <math id="A2.SS6.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}(\gamma^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}(\gamma^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A2.SS6.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">By summing over all <math id="A2.SS6.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and following Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> as well as the proof in case <math id="A2.SS6.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}\in\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}\in\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain
<math id="A2.SS6.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{est}/\alpha\geq(1-O(\epsilon+\delta))C_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{est}/\alpha\geq(1-O(\epsilon+\delta))C_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS6.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C_{alg}-C_{est}/\alpha|\leq\left(O(\delta)+O\left(\epsilon^{3/2}\sqrt{\delta/\alpha}\right)\right)C_{est}/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{alg}-C_{est}/\alpha|\leq\left(O(\delta)+O\left(\epsilon^{3/2}\sqrt{\delta/\alpha}\right)\right)C_{est}/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, <a href="#alg1" title="In 2 Background and Formal Problem Setup ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> satisfies that <math id="A2.SS6.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{alg}}{C_{opt}}\geq 1-O(\epsilon+\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{alg}}{C_{opt}}\geq 1-O(\epsilon+\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>More Experiment Results</h2>

<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.02718v1/order_worst.svg" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/119;" width="476" height="119"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A3.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results under the worst-case query order, where queries are sorted in descending order of cost.
(Left to right): the first three subfigures correspond to RouterBench, the next three to SPROUT, and the last three to Open LLM Leaderboard v2.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.02718v1/M.svg" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/294;" width="476" height="294"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A3.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results when varying the configurations of deployed LLMs.
Rows correspond to different datasets: RouterBench (top), SPROUT (middle), and Open LLM Leaderboard v2 (bottom).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Query Arrival Order</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the robustness of our algorithm under varying query arrival orders.
Specifically, we consider two settings:
(1) a randomized setting, where test queries are independently shuffled 100 times to reflect realistic, unpredictable online environments; and
(2) a worst-case setting, where queries are sorted in descending order of their maximum cost across all models.
This adversarial order simulates scenarios in which expensive queries arrive early and are more likely to exhaust the budget.
Figure <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 5 Evaluation ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows that our algorithm consistently outperforms all baselines across metrics and benchmarks under random permutations.
Even under the worst-case order (Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix C More Experiment Results ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), our method maintains the advantage, achieving the best performance across all metrics on SPROUT and Open LLM Leaderboard v2, and outperforming all baselines in terms of performance and cost-efficiency on RouterBench.
These results demonstrate the robustness of our algorithm towards varying query orders.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.02718v1/extreme.svg" id="A3.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/294;" width="476" height="294"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A3.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results under the extreme budget split.
Rows correspond to different datasets: RouterBench (top), SPROUT (middle), and Open LLM Leaderboard v2 (bottom).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F10" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.02718v1/budget.svg" id="A3.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/294;" width="476" height="294"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="A3.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results when varying total budget <math id="A3.F10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> from 0.25 to 2<math id="A3.F10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> the cost of the cheapest model. Rows correspond to different datasets: RouterBench (top), SPROUT (middle), and Open LLM Leaderboard v2 (bottom).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Scalability to LLM Deployments.</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One of the key advantages of our algorithm is its scalability to varying configurations of LLM deployments.
To evaluate the robustness of our algorithm, we vary the configurations of deployed LLMs on each benchmark.
For RouterBench, which includes 11 distinct LLMs in total, we vary the deployed LLMs from 2 to 8.
For SPROUT, which has 13 different LLMs, we vary the deployed LLMs from 2 to 10.
For Open LLM Leaderboard v2, which includes 18 distinct models, we vary the number of deployed LLMs from 2 to 16.
In all settings where the number of deployed LLMs is fewer than the maximum, we randomly sample the deployed LLMs and repeat the experiment 10 times to ensure diversity and coverage of possible configurations.
Note that in this experiment, we compare only against training-free methods, as retraining models used in model-based methods for each of the numerous settings would incur significant computational and deployment overhead.
As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Appendix C More Experiment Results ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, our algorithm consistently achieves strong performance across all deployment configurations, where the cost-efficiency gap over other baselines steadily increases.
These results demonstrate the robustness and adaptability of our method to diverse and dynamic LLM serving environments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F11" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.02718v1/base.svg" id="A3.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/295;" width="476" height="295"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A3.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results when varying the number of historical data points.
Rows correspond to different datasets: RouterBench (top), SPROUT (middle), and
Open LLM Leaderboard v2 (bottom).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F12" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.02718v1/topk.svg" id="A3.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/294;" width="476" height="294"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="A3.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results when varying the number of search candidates.
Rows correspond to different datasets: RouterBench (top), SPROUT (middle), and Open LLM Leaderboard v2
(bottom).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Budget Split</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One key factor affecting the performance of routing algorithms is the choice of budget split strategy.
We extend the default cost-efficiency-based split to five alternative strategies.
As shown in Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.1 Robustness ‣ 5 Evaluation ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, our algorithm consistently outperforms all baselines across all benchmarks and metrics under four different split strategies: cost-based, performance-based, uniform, and random.
Even under the extreme split setting (Figure <a href="#A3.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ C.1 Query Arrival Order ‣ Appendix C More Experiment Results ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), where a large portion of the budget is concentrated on a few low-efficiency models, our method maintains leading performance.
Notably, when 80% of the budget is allocated to a single model (<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math>), our algorithm achieves nearly <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></span> the performance of the strongest baseline (BatchSplit) on the RouterBench.
On Open LLM Leaderboard v2, it also demonstrates approximately <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></span> higher cost efficiency than all baselines.
These results underscore the strong robustness and adaptability of our algorithm against a wide range of complex and imbalanced budget allocation schemes.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F13" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.02718v1/embed.svg" id="A3.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/171;" width="476" height="171"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F13.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 13</span>: </span><span id="A3.F13.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results using different embedding models. Each group of 9 subfigures corresponds
to one embedding: (a) gte-Qwen2-1.5B-instruct (subfigures 1–9), (b) SFR-Embedding-2_R (subfigures 10–18). Within each group, the first three subfigures correspond to RouterBench, the next three to SPROUT, and the last three to Open LLM Leaderboard v2.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F14" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.02718v1/alpha_eps.svg" id="A3.F14.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/295;" width="476" height="295"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F14.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 14</span>: </span><span id="A3.F14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Results when varying <math id="A3.F14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.F14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Rows
correspond to different datasets: RouterBench (top), SPROUT (middle), and Open LLM Leaderboard v2 (bottom).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Total Budget</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the performance of our algorithms in different budget settings, we scale the total budget <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> from 0.25 to 2<math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> the cost of the cheapest model.
Results shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ C.1 Query Arrival Order ‣ Appendix C More Experiment Results ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> demonstrate that our algorithm achieves competitive or superior performance compared to all baselines across benchmarks and metrics.
Notably, even under the extremely constrained budget, it maintains a clear advantage.
For instance, at <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=0.25</annotation></semantics></math>, it achieves nearly <span id="A3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2<math id="A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></span> the performance and cost efficiency of the strongest baseline (BatchSplit) on the Open LLM Leaderboard v2.
These results underscore the robustness of our method and its adaptability to different resource availability scenarios.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Historical Data Size &amp; ANNS/KNN Candidates</h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Historical Data Size.</span>
To evaluate the robustness of our algorithm with respect to the size of historical data, we vary the number of historical data points used in ANNS and KNN from 5000 to 25000.
For RouterBench, whose maximum available historical data is 26497, we randomly sample the subset of data points from 5000 to 25000.
For RouterBench, which contains up to 26497 historical records, we randomly sample subsets within this range.
For SPROUT, with a maximum of 30968 records, we similarly sample subsets from 5000 to 25000.
For Open LLM Leaderboard v2, which has 11065 historical records, we sample subsets ranging from 5000 to 10000.
Note that in this experiment, training-based methods are trained on the full historical dataset to provide a strong baseline for comparison.
As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ C.2 Scalability to LLM Deployments. ‣ Appendix C More Experiment Results ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, the results clearly show that varying the amount of historical data used in ANNS and KNN has minimal impact on performance, with our algorithm consistently and significantly outperforming all baselines across all settings.
This demonstrates the robustness and efficiency of our algorithm: even with as few as 5000 historical records, it remains effective for routing.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Number of ANNS/KNN Candidates.</span>
To investigate the impact of the number of search candidates of ANNS and KNN on routing performance, we vary the candidate pool size from the default 5 to 3, 7, and 10.
As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ C.2 Scalability to LLM Deployments. ‣ Appendix C More Experiment Results ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, the results show that performance is marginally affected, with a slight improvement as the candidate pool size increases.
Notably, our algorithm consistently maintains a leading position across all settings.
Even with as few as 3 search candidates, it outperforms all baselines across benchmarks, demonstrating its stability and robustness to the choice of candidate pool size.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F15" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.02718v1/routerbench_heat.png" id="A3.F15.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/294;" width="429" height="294" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F15.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 15</span>: </span><span id="A3.F15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results across different query types in RouterBench.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.6 </span>Detailed Ablation Study</h3>

<div id="A3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Impact of embedding models.</span>
The choice of embedding model is also important for estimating the performance score and cost of incoming queries.
To evaluate the adaptivity of our algorithm to different embedding models used in ANNS, we conduct experiments with two larger embedding models: <span id="A3.SS6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SFR-Embedding-2_R</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> and <span id="A3.SS6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gte-Qwen2-1.5B-instruct</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>.
As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ C.3 Budget Split ‣ Appendix C More Experiment Results ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, our algorithm consistently outperforms all baselines across all benchmarks, demonstrating its robustness to the choice of embedding model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Impact of <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
We evaluate the sensitivity of our method to the parameters <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, as shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ C.3 Budget Split ‣ Appendix C More Experiment Results ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>.
For <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, we observe a consistent decline in performance as it increases, with the best result achieved at <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.0001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.0001</annotation></semantics></math>.
This trend aligns with Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 4 Theoretical Guarantees ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, which shows that a larger <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> amplifies the gap between the performance of our algorithm on the observed subset <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\hat{C}}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\hat{C}}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>, and its expected value <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon{\hat{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon{\hat{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This increased discrepancy results in greater deviation in performance on future queries, ultimately leading to a reduction in overall performance on the full query set <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the parameter <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we observe that increasing its value initially improves performance, reaching a peak at around <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.025" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.025</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.025</annotation></semantics></math>, after which further increases lead to a decline.
This aligns with the intuition that <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> controls the number of samples used in the learning stage: too few samples lead to underfitting, while too many may lead to overfitting to the observed data.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F16" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.02718v1/sprout_heat.png" id="A3.F16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/253;" width="429" height="253" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F16.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 16</span>: </span><span id="A3.F16.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Results across different query types in SPROUT.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F17" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.02718v1/leaderboard_heat.png" id="A3.F17.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/257;" width="429" height="257" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F17.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 17</span>: </span><span id="A3.F17.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Results across different query types in Open LLM Leaderboard v2.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.7 </span>Routing Analysis by Query Types</h3>

<div id="A3.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To gain deeper insights into how our algorithm routes different types of queries, we analyze its routing behavior across the three benchmarks.
We categorize query types based on their data sources, as each source is designed to evaluate different LLM capabilities.
As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ C.5 Historical Data Size &amp; ANNS/KNN Candidates ‣ Appendix C More Experiment Results ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, <a href="#A3.F16" title="Figure 16 ‣ C.6 Detailed Ablation Study ‣ Appendix C More Experiment Results ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, and <a href="#A3.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ C.6 Detailed Ablation Study ‣ Appendix C More Experiment Results ‣ Efficient Training-Free Online Routing for High-Volume Multi-LLM Serving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, our algorithm consistently achieves superior or competitive routing performance in most query types across benchmarks.
These results demonstrate the generalizability and effectiveness of our algorithm in handling diverse query types, which indicates that its performance is not dependent on a narrow subset of tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Extended Related Work</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM Routing.</span>
Existing LLM routing research primarily falls into two paradigms.
The first focuses on improving response quality while managing cost, typically through ensembling outputs from different LLMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite> or using cascading strategies that query LLMs sequentially based on their capabilities <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>.
For instance, LLM-Blender <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> proposes an ensembling framework that combines outputs from multiple open-source LLMs and selects the optimal response.
 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite>using outputs
Wang et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite> propose to fuse outputs of expert models that capture complementary aspects of the data distribution, to generate the final answer.
Frugal-GPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> adopts a sequential querying strategy, invoking LLMs in order of increasing capability until a satisfactory response is obtained.
AutoMix <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> first uses a smaller model to self-verify the quality of the response, based on which it dynamically selects a suitably sized model for handling the query.
Although these approaches can improve performance, they incur high latency and computational cost due to multiple model invocations per query.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The second paradigm leverages historical or auxiliary datasets to estimate the performance and cost of each query and select the optimal LLM accordingly <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, <a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>, <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>.
In this line of work, several approaches train model-based predictors using these labeled historical datasets.
For example, RouterLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite> trains a BERT-base or causal LLM on the historical data annotated with human preferences to enhance routing accuracy.
CARROT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite> trains Roberta-base models to estimate both performance and cost for each query, enabling selection of the optimal LLM under any user-defined trade-off between quality and cost.
HybridLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> adopts the synthetic preference labels from the MixInstruct dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> based on BARTScore <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>, and trains a single BERT-based router for query routing.
Zooter <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite> distills reward signals from training queries and applies tag-based label enhancement to train a routing function that facilitates the expert selection.
TensorOpera <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite> introduces a soft label-based strategy based on the BERT similarity scores to train the BERT-based predictor for query routing.
GraphRouter <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite> constructs a heterogeneous graph to capture the contextual relationship between the query requirements and the LLM capabilities for informed routing decisions.
While these training-based approaches are effective for certain LLM deployment settings, they introduce nontrivial training overhead.
Furthermore, adapting them to varying LLM deployment configurations typically requires retraining, which makes them unsuitable for resource-constrained online routing with diverse LLM deployment configurations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Some methods avoid training by using approaches such as KNN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite> or similarity-weighted (SW) ranking <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite> to estimate the performance and cost based on the historical data.
While these approaches avoid model training overhead, they still incur substantial computational overhead and latency, as they rely on brute-force comparisons against the entire historical dataset to retrieve similar examples or compute similarity scores without any optimization.
Specifically, they operate with a high search complexity of <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the size of the dataset.
As a result, these methods are difficult to scale and impractical for high-volume, budget-constrained online routing scenarios.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Recent efforts <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite> have explored formulating LLM routing as MILP.
For instance, Sakota et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite> introduce two MILP-based strategies, targeting performance-oriented and cost-oriented, respectively.
However, these methods face significant challenges in high-volume online routing settings, where queries arrive sequentially, rather than simultaneously, making the offline optimal infeasible to compute.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We complement these works by introducing the first training-free and efficient online routing method with provable performance guarantees, tailored for high-volume, budget-constrained, and dynamic LLM-serving environments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Online Matching.</span>
This problem has been extensively studied for decades, with much of the literature focusing on important special cases of the general online submodular welfare maximization problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>.
These include the classical unweighted online bipartite matching problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>, its extension to vertex-weighted matching <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, the display ads allocation problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, and the AdWords problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
